{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 43, :comments ["<b>And Moses saw all the work.</b> This is the work of the Tabernacle. And the sense of וירא, 'and he saw,' is: he saw on the mountain, in the manner of what is written (Exodus 25:9): ״ככל אשר אני מראה אותך״ — 'according to all that I show you' — and it is written (ibid.): ״אשר אתה מראה בהר״ — 'which you are shown on the mountain' — and behold, they made it, in the wilderness." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> ״וירא משה את כל המלאכה״ — 'And Moses saw all the work' — this is the work of Creation. It does not say ״את כל מלאכת המשכן״ — 'all the work of the Tabernacle' — but only thus, to teach you that the work of the Tabernacle is weighed against the act of Creation. Immediately: ״ויברך אותם משה״ — 'and Moses blessed them.' What blessing did he bless them? He said: May it be the will that the Shekhinah rest upon the work of your hands. Immediately he said (Psalms 90:17): ״והי נעם ה' אלהינו עלינו ומעשה ידינו כוננה עלינו״ — 'May the pleasantness of HaShem our Elohim be upon us, and the work of our hands establish it for us' — because its beginning is (ibid.): ״תפלה למשה איש האלהים״ — 'A prayer of Moses, the man of Elohim.' And the sense of ״מעשה ידינו״ — 'the work of our hands' — is the raising of the hands that Aaron performed on the day of the erection, for this is the language of עלינו, 'upon us'; and ״מעשה ידינו כוננהו״ is for the success of the work of their hands, and not according to the opinion of Rabbi David Kimhi, of blessed memory, who explained that it is an expression of duplication."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:08:01.799728812Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}